Since, $n(A \cap B)=99n((A \times B) \cap(B \times A))$
\begin{aligned}
&=n((A \cap B) \times(B \cap A)) \\
&=n(A \cap B) \cdot n(B \cap A) \\
&=n(A \cap B) \cdot n(A \cap B)=99 \cdot 99=(99)^{2}
\end{aligned}

Let $\quad \mathrm{C}=\mathrm{A} \cap \mathrm{B}$, then
$C \times C=(A \cap B) \times(A \cap B)=(A \cap B) \times(B \cap A)$
\begin{gathered}
=(A \times B) \cap(B \times A) \\
{[\because(A \cap C) \times(B \cap D)=(A \times B) \cap(C \times D)]}
